{
  "id": "Lyo.MessageQueue.RabbitMq.Web.Components",
  "name": "Lyo.MessageQueue.RabbitMq.Web.Components",
  "area": "Communication",
  "tagline": "Blazor UI for RabbitMQ exchanges, bindings, and broker workbenches.",
  "description": "Blazor UI for RabbitMQ exchanges, bindings, and broker workbenches.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "RabbitMqWorkbench",
      "headers": [
        "Tab",
        "Operations"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**Queues**",
          "Type-to-filter dropdown (name plus flag chips in the list). **Info** shows durable/state/type chips plus ready/unacked/consumers. **Quick actions** peek/clear/delete/copy. Inner **Send** tab: wrap/priority/delay/send. Inner **Manage** tab: create and bind."
        ],
        [
          "**Exchanges**",
          "Type-to-filter dropdown (name plus type/durable chips). `amq.*` and the unnamed default stay hidden unless Show defaults is on. **Info** and **Quick actions** sit side by side. Inner **Send** tab: wrap/priority/delay/routing key/send. Inner **Manage** tab: create and bind."
        ]
      ],
      "lead": "`RabbitMqWorkbench` is a list-select dashboard for the full `IRabbitMqService` API. Queue and exchange snapshots load on the first render. Auto-refresh remains on the queue toolbar.",
      "trail": "Creating a queue supports:\n\n- **`x-max-priority`.** Numeric max priority (same pattern as job workers use for `job.run.{workerType}` queues).\n- **DLQ auto-wiring.** `CreateQueueWithDlq` with optional custom DLQ name.\n\nPublish supports:\n\n- **`SendToQueueWithPriority`.** Envelope publish with priority (requires a priority-enabled queue).\n- **`SendToQueueDelayed`.** Broker-side delay via TTL + dead-letter wait queues."
    }
  ],
